id: pm-43p2c3
title: "GitHub managed-package update checks report git's command line and stderr as update_error instead of a stable code, and a timed-out ls-remote looks like any other failure"
description: "Found while fixing pm-5kfzjh. checkGithubUpdate in src/sdk/extension/update-check.ts reports error.message from runGitCommand as update_error, and the extension summary repeats it as update_check_reason. runGitCommand (src/sdk/extension/install-sources.ts) builds that message as \"Git command failed: git ls-remote <repository> <ref> <ref>^{}\" followed by git's stderr, or by execFile's own \"Command failed\" text. A GitHub update check therefore reports a multi-line string, not a stable code. Callers cannot branch on it, and it repeats git's stderr, which can name proxy hosts, credential helper prompts or local paths. A lookup killed by its budget is not told apart from a missing repository, the same gap pm-5kfzjh closed for npm. The npm path reports stable codes (npm_registry_lookup_failed, npm_registry_lookup_timed_out with update_check_timeout_ms). The GitHub path should do the same, with codes such as github_remote_lookup_failed and github_remote_lookup_timed_out, while keeping no_remote_reference_found and missing_installed_commit."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 3
tags[5]: diagnostics,extensions,github,stable-codes,update-check
created_at: "2026-11-18T09:38:17.161Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-18T11:26:01.910Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-18T11:26:00.887Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-18T11:26:00.887Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: "A failed GitHub update check reports a stable update_error code, never git's command line, repository URL or stderr; a git ls-remote lookup killed by its budget reports a distinct timed-out code and names the budget in update_check_timeout_ms, as the npm path does; unit tests cover the timeout, failure and success classifications; docs/PACKAGE_EVIDENCE.md lists the GitHub codes"
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: low
resolution: "checkGithubUpdate's default runner runs git ls-remote through runBoundedUpdateQuery with GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 and GCM_INTERACTIVE=never. It reports github_remote_lookup_timed_out with update_check_timeout_ms when the deadline passes, and github_remote_lookup_failed for any other failure, never git's command line, the repository URL or stderr. An injected runner takes (args, timeoutMs). no_remote_reference_found and missing_installed_commit are unchanged. docs/PACKAGE_EVIDENCE.md lists the codes, and a contract_change declares the migration."
expected_result: "A GitHub update check failure is a stable, private-data-free code that tells a timeout apart from an unavailable remote"
actual_result: "Unit tests assert both codes and that a failed status contains no ls-remote, repository host or stderr; a real fake-git integration test settles a stalled lookup in about 1 s as github_remote_lookup_timed_out and kills its descendant"
component: extensions
